    <data key="d0">MakeMyTrip: Next-Gen SOC with Apache Metron and a Security Data Lake</data>
    <data key="d1">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-3lnf5lzsH0</data>
    <data key="d2">MakeMyTrip built a next-gen SOC from the ground up to detect abnormal behaviour beyond signature/rule-based detection. Hybrid data ingest (public cloud and on-prem) feeds Apache Metron (parsing, enrichment, profiling). A serverless security data lake (EMR, S3, Athena) stores telemetry for months/years and feeds long-term profiles back to Metron. A SOAR platform (Blitz, open source) handles incident response and semi-automated mitigation (e.g. WAF blocking). Scale: about 20 data sources, about 5000 events per second, about 250 million events indexed per day. Example use case: detecting server compromise through deviation of the producer-consumer ratio (PCR). Next step: threat hunting on the data lake.</data>
    <data key="d3">Security, Analytics, Data Lake, Incident Response</data>
    <data key="d4">True</data>
  </graph>
</graphml>
